          },
          "description": "Even a monarch needs a best friend, and Queen Elizabeth II found one in a corgi pup named Susan. From princesshood to queendom, the pair forged an unbreakable bond, with Susan even participating in Elizabeth’s wedding day and joining her on her honeymoon with Prince Philip. Over the course of her remarkable seventy-year reign, the Queen had more than thirty corgi companions, and almost all of them were direct descendants of her cherished Susan.  \n\n<b>A Macmillan Audio production from Godwin Books.</b>",
          "author": "Caroline L. Perry",
